{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. You're in the ICU. You were brought in because you were confused and not making sense to your family. Do you remember what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I... I don’t really remember. I was sick, throwing up dark stuff. My son called someone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your son called 911. You were in diabetic ketoacidosis—your blood sugar was extremely high, over 1200, and your body was very acidic. We’ve started treatment with IV fluids and insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:20:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh no... again? I know I haven’t been checking my sugar. My meter broke, and I didn’t get a new one."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:21:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s part of it. Your potassium was dangerously high too, and your kidneys weren’t working well. We gave you medicine to protect your heart and help lower the potassium."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:23:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so weak. Did I need a breathing tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:24:50",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. When you came in, you were breathing fast but starting to tire. Your blood gases showed worsening acidosis and rising CO2, so we had to intubate to support your breathing. You’re on a ventilator now but doing much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:26:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m scared. Is my heart okay? I’ve had issues before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re concerned you had a mild heart attack—what we call an NSTEMI. It’s likely due to the stress of DKA and your underlying heart disease. Your troponin went up a bit, but your echo showed your heart is pumping strongly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:30:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no damage? I’ve had two heart attacks before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:31:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The damage appears small. Your heart function is actually hyperdynamic—pumping harder than normal. But because of your history of not taking medications consistently, cardiology decided medications are safer than procedures right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:33:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I mess up. I stop taking things when I feel bad or can’t afford them. And I’ve been drinking less, but it’s hard."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. That’s why we’ve involved psychiatry. They think starting a new antidepressant—Zoloft—will help, and they recommend a partial hospitalization program for depression and alcohol use."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:36:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve tried that before. I didn’t stick with it. But maybe this time..."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2162-05-03 10:38:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll support you. You’ve already agreed to the program, and your family is involved. That’s a big step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2162-05-03 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your labs are improving. Your acid levels are correcting, and your potassium is down to 5.1. We’ve turned off the insulin drip and started you back on long-acting insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2162-05-03 14:22:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I eat soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2162-05-03 14:23:40",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re removing the breathing tube soon. Once you’re breathing on your own and tolerating food, we’ll move you out of the ICU. Your kidney function is also improving—creatinine is down to 1.8 from 2.8."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2162-05-03 14:25:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember they put a dialysis line in. Did I need dialysis?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2162-05-03 14:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We used it for ultrafiltration to help your kidneys rest. But you responded well to fluids and insulin, so no ongoing dialysis is needed. Your urine output has improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2162-05-03 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re off the ventilator now and doing well. We’re transferring you to the medical floor tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2162-05-03 18:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel more like myself. But I’m still tired."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2162-05-03 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s expected. Your body went through a lot. Your white count was high at first but is now coming down. We’re confident there’s no infection—your cultures were negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2162-05-04 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar is still a bit high—around 350—but much better. We’ve started a sliding scale with fast-acting insulin before meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2162-05-04 09:07:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I need to get back to checking it myself. Can I use my old meter?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2162-05-04 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re sending you home with a new FreeStyle Lite meter and strips. You’ll check four times a day. Also, we’re adjusting your insulin: 16 units of glargine at breakfast, 2 at bedtime, plus sliding scale as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2162-05-04 09:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was supposed to start an insulin pump last time. I never did."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2162-05-04 09:13:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We discussed that. Given your current stability and the need to rebuild routine, we think injections are safer for now. We can revisit the pump later with your endocrinologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2162-05-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning are excellent. Glucose is 180, potassium 4.3, bicarbonate 24. Your kidney function has normalized—creatinine is 0.7."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2162-05-05 10:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my heart meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2162-05-05 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re now on metoprolol, aspirin, and atorvastatin—important for heart protection. We restarted your lisinopril and amlodipine for blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2162-05-05 10:06:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I used to take Effexor and mirtazapine. What happened to those?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2162-05-05 10:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry recommended switching to Zoloft. Mirtazapine can increase appetite and weight, which is harder with diabetes. Effexor was tapered off. You’ll take Zoloft daily now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2162-05-06 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing so well. Walking, eating, managing your insulin. We’re planning for discharge in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2162-05-06 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m nervous about going home. What if I fall back into old habits?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2162-05-06 09:34:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s why the partial program is key. It’s daily therapy for both depression and alcohol use. You start in two days. Your daughter will help you get there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2162-05-07 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin is stable, slightly low at 7.7. We think it’s from long-term alcohol use. You’re on folic acid and iron, which should help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2162-05-07 10:17:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had a drink in over a week. I want to keep it that way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2162-05-07 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a huge accomplishment. The program will support your sobriety. And your white count is low but stable—likely just a variant. We’ll check it as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2162-05-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we’re focusing on discharge prep. You’ll go home with visiting nurse services to check on you daily for the first week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2162-05-08 09:02:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I live alone, but my daughter’s close."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2162-05-08 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "She’s listed as your emergency contact. You have follow-up with primary care, endocrinology, cardiology, and the addiction service."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2162-05-09 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your last labs look great. Glucose 150, creatinine 0.6, potassium 4.2. We’re clearing you for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2162-05-09 10:22:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I can’t believe it. I was so sick just days ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2162-05-09 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve worked hard. Keep up the insulin checks, take all your meds, and go to every appointment. The program is your best chance to stay healthy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2162-05-10 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re officially discharged today. Here’s your medication list and prescriptions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2162-05-10 08:32:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’ll start the partial program Monday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2162-05-10 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. If you feel worse—shortness of breath, chest pain, confusion—go to the ER. Otherwise, see your PCP in one week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2162-05-10 08:36:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I want to get this right this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2162-05-10 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We believe you can. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2162-05-11 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, it’s Dr. Lee. Just checking in. How are you feeling at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2162-05-11 14:02:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired, but okay. I’m checking my sugar like I should. It’s been between 140 and 200."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2162-05-11 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good control. Any nausea or trouble breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2162-05-11 14:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, just a little sore from the IV lines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2162-05-11 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That should fade. Keep up the good work. See you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2162-05-12 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your visiting nurse reported you’re doing well—eating, walking, taking meds. That’s great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2162-05-12 09:17:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m trying. The Zoloft makes me a little nauseous in the morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2162-05-12 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Try taking it with breakfast. If it continues, call your psychiatrist. Otherwise, keep going."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2162-05-13 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One day until your program starts. Any concerns?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2162-05-13 10:02:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just nervous. But I know I need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2162-05-13 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s normal. You’re not alone. We’re all rooting for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2162-05-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m calling to wish you well on your first day of the program. You’ve come so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2162-05-14 09:02:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I’m heading out now. I’m going to do this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2162-05-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know you will. Take care of yourself."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2162-05-03 09:56:00",
    "admission_end": "2162-05-14 19:02:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of type 1 diabetes, poorly controlled due to medication noncompliance, alcohol use disorder, and depression, presented with altered mental status and was found to be in severe diabetic ketoacidosis with a glucose of 1214, pH of 6.92, and anion gap of 56. She had hyperkalemia, acute kidney injury with creatinine rising to 2.8, and hypotension requiring pressor support. Due to worsening acidosis and respiratory fatigue, she was intubated and admitted to the MICU. She received an insulin drip, IV fluids, bicarbonate, and temporary hemodialysis via a right internal jugular line. Her course improved with correction of metabolic abnormalities, and she was transitioned to subcutaneous insulin. She had a non-ST elevation myocardial infarction likely due to demand ischemia, managed medically with metoprolol, aspirin, and atorvastatin. Psychiatry initiated Zoloft and arranged for a dual-diagnosis partial hospitalization program. Her renal function recovered, and she was discharged home with services, improved mental status, and a plan for ongoing behavioral and medical follow-up.",
    "problems": [
